{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "articulated-lamp",
  "subject": "A burgundy articulated desk-lamp robot with a brass shade, warm bulb, paired hinge bars and a cream work pad.",
  "style": "Polished retro-industrial desk toy with rounded joints, metallic brass details and readable mechanical articulation.",
  "prompt": "Create a complete editable desk-lamp robot, distinct from a creature or humanoid. Use a stable burgundy circular base, twin-bar lower and upper arms, brass hinge caps, a tapered brass shade and an opaque warm-colored bulb. Keep the base, arm lengths and shade proportions consistent in all states. Idle is a small curious look-around; making_something is a precise repeated shade-tip tracing gesture over its work pad; working is a slow wide inspection scan; milestone_level_up is a proud upright stretch and double head nod. Author hidden mechanical surfaces, pivots and rigid skin weights explicitly. Do not claim real light emission, dynamic ink, physical dynamics or reference reconstruction.",
  "authored_assumptions": [
    "Original full 3D design assembled from smooth primitives; no external reference.",
    "All joints are authored mechanical pivots with rigid weights, not a simulated linkage constraint system.",
    "The warm bulb is opaque colored geometry, not volumetric light or a luminous beam.",
    "Tracing and inspection are gestural animations over a static work pad; no ink or manufacturing is simulated.",
    "Keyframe rotations and translations are expressed in model rest axes (X right, Y rear, Z up). The builder converts these offsets through each bone rest basis before writing Blender pose transforms."
  ],
